 "notes": "index.csv/chunk call this Gilbert Almquist, Commission Seat C, 2016. The cover's 'Full Name of Candidate' reads 'Gilbert Almquist' and its 'Office' line reads 'Washington County Commissioner seat C', with the added line 'This office includes all areas of Washington County.' - a county office, IN SCOPE; agrees with the chunk file. Addressed 'TO: County Clerk: Melanie Abplanalp'; RECEIVED JUN 17 2016 WASHINGTON COUNTY CLERK-AUDITOR stamp; certification period 25-Jan-2016 to 06-17-16, dated 17 June 2016. THE PDF HAS NO TEXT LAYER (pdftotext returns 5 bytes) despite being typed, which is why it sits in the image-faced queue; every value here was read from the page image, never from OCR. ⚠ The chunk file gives n_reports=1 and I see ONE report across 5 pages - the extra pages are schedule continuations, not stapled reports. Privacy: the cover prints the candidate's street address, home phone and cell phone, and EVERY Form A row prints a full street address - all discarded at read time; only city and state were kept, verbatim as typed ('St. George', 'Utah', 'Texas', 'NC', 'SLC', 'New Harmony'). The Form A heading carries an 'In Kind?' column and the filer answered it on NO row, so in_kind is false everywhere with the column left blank - a blank is not an 'N'. Three donors are the candidate or his household, and four rows are the candidate reimbursing himself; they are itemized as contributions by the filer and transcribed as he filed them.",
